From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:49:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 49/53] wayland: deliver the cursor rectangle of text inputs
 focused after another

A cursor rectangle waits for the surface's next state before it reaches
the input method. When focus moved on before that, such as when the
window closed, the handler stayed recorded on the old surface, so no
text input focused afterwards ever told the input method where its
cursor is. Drop the pending update when focus leaves the surface.

Upstream-Status: forwardable
---
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c
index f12f9f3a53f5fa9fa30487a3095fe778b2240be3..0aafcfe77ecb6a53337d24eca10363c6e95d3dcd 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c
@@ -577,6 +577,8 @@ meta_wayland_text_input_set_focus (MetaWaylandTextInput *text_input,
           reset_text_input_focus (text_input);
         }
 
+      g_clear_signal_handler (&text_input->cursor_update.signal_id,
+                              text_input->surface);
       wl_list_remove (&text_input->surface_listener.link);
       text_input->surface = NULL;
       /* Wayland set_surrounding_text() does not support to set null string
